    "updated_at": "2026-08-15T23:58:29.741064"
   },
   {
    "id": "it_a754a6738d65",
    "card": "timeline",
    "text": "Discussing emailing results: entering an email address so the app mails you; OCR may not be available on this computer.",
    "data": {
     "start_s": 1085.6
    },
    "status": "proposed",
    "author_type": "agent",
    "author_id": "agent",
    "pinned": false,
    "revision": 1,
    "evidence": [
     "sg_cdff2e1de32a3fb95985",
     "sg_36c88acb3fd13c9120be",
     "sg_c8035d5741e08924be43"
    ],
    "created_at": "2026-08-15T23:59:23.615702",
    "updated_at": "2026-08-15T23:59:23.615702"
   },
   {
    "id": "it_5f5ffdee2d80",
    "card": "timeline",
    "text": "Everything is based on MATLAB; for online real-time use MATLAB isn't trusted, so it has to be coded.",
    "data": {
     "start_s": 1125.0
    },
    "status": "proposed",
    "author_type": "agent",
    "author_id": "agent",
    "pinned": false,
    "revision": 1,
    "evidence": [
     "sg_da4fb8183489e87fd65d",
     "sg_03f7662dfdf583a7af77",
     "sg_9819a027c743df174ca1",
     "sg_552139a96a82685736b9"
    ],
    "created_at": "2026-08-15T23:59:23.615702",
    "updated_at": "2026-08-15T23:59:23.615702"
   }
  ],
  "live_notes": [
   {
    "id": "it_11bb0408ee4a",
    "card": "live_notes",
    "text": "These measures quantify involvement in the discussion and are not expensive to compute; the more expensive part is the final decision \u2014 identifying who is speaking or tracking a person who moved, the most complicated case being someone leaving and returning to a different seat. Statistical models of person identity would need to be built from these measures.",
    "data": {
     "heading": "Measures: cost and decision complexity",
     "start_s": 245.2
    },
    "status": "proposed",
    "author_type": "agent",
    "author_id": "agent",
    "pinned": false,
    "revision": 1,
    "evidence": [
     "sg_e566d9e39d35d0d7bbb8",
     "sg_b31d29c151ab15d9e200",
     "sg_353ce3fbd6f223b7abb2",
     "sg_1d0e4edd36948a6b81e9",
     "sg_7afc463c03ee11d65917",
     "sg_f72c06a74c9cb9dabd19",
     "sg_e8d03ae809de5e54c35f",
     "sg_da34ebdae1c3799edc5b"
    ],
    "created_at": "2026-08-15T23:45:09.330869",
    "updated_at": "2026-08-15T23:45:09.330869"
   },
   {
    "id": "it_ab9cd209278b",
    "card": "live_notes",
    "text": "Processing is done via FFT; these measures evaluate a person's identity. Location alone only extracts speech segments and clusters of where noise regularly comes from \u2014 it cannot tell that segments come from the same person. Location may suffice for short periods (e.g., 10 minutes) or a fixed setting like the current room, but the target deployment is a flexible place where people move, so more than location is needed.",
    "data": {
     "heading": "Location vs identity limits",
     "start_s": 340.9
    },
    "status": "proposed",
    "author_type": "agent",
    "author_id": "agent",
    "pinned": false,
    "revision": 1,
    "evidence": [
     "sg_d03af11e62030efdc78d",
     "sg_12d95b6b00014012869a",
     "sg_6652b904ee4fd7c4f8da",
     "sg_0a0034a01e3ffd40a5ee",
     "sg_63bbe242514e972911ca",
     "sg_162e6eeb42d115f5296c",
     "sg_9d9de6a5f07f1363f93a",
     "sg_9633b7a125188bec67a5",
     "sg_060a86f647f0405f4850",
     "sg_a93bba0466bfc9865de5"
    ],
    "created_at": "2026-08-15T23:45:09.330869",
    "updated_at": "2026-08-15T23:45:09.330869"
   },
   {
    "id": "it_9ea40d391ce5",
    "card": "live_notes",
    "text": "Debate on whether knowing which person is speaking matters: for a physical table, knowing which cone/position speech comes from may be enough, but identity is important for detecting patterns such as how much a person spoke over the last five minutes. The measures could be used simply online to give feedback, while another side of the project analyzes data offline.",
    "data": {
     "heading": "Identity value; online vs offline use",
     "start_s": 411.6
    },
    "status": "proposed",
    "author_type": "agent",
    "author_id": "agent",
    "pinned": false,
    "revision": 1,
    "evidence": [
     "sg_018dda27aea47132066b",
     "sg_fb5e608a99cb250e2517",
     "sg_48624f8a2dd4c9136f09",
     "sg_e88fe3622b44122cea7f",
     "sg_925cddddff70178e7985",
     "sg_1d131e12f5e9d0a74499",
     "sg_2bc9496d7391d81c0725",
     "sg_f212d4624efaeb117eaa"
    ],
    "created_at": "2026-08-15T23:45:09.330869",
    "updated_at": "2026-08-15T23:45:09.330869"
   },
   {
    "id": "it_16b826ac2d57",
    "card": "live_notes",
    "text": "Extracting the words spoken adds semantic context (e.g., detecting that someone is angry about a word). Keyword spotting could trigger events \u2014 for instance, a professor being alerted when people talk about him. Noted as a possible future direction, not part of the current project scope.",
    "data": {
     "heading": "Keyword spotting and semantic context",
     "start_s": 739.3
    },
    "status": "proposed",
    "author_type": "agent",
    "author_id": "agent",
    "pinned": false,
    "revision": 1,
    "evidence": [
     "sg_5085e8afc179b7205411",
     "sg_19e1adc31555dbd16225",
     "sg_c16e01cd355aaa548f0b",
     "sg_5d757b67185a782128aa",
     "sg_06bba96347dc9e9a5a66",
     "sg_04e4e679695684908039",
     "sg_f437caf7ae73686d9480",
     "sg_d20d86c340db787dd7d8",
     "sg_3374f472de03b12e21c1"
    ],
    "created_at": "2026-08-15T23:57:17.146917",
    "updated_at": "2026-08-15T23:57:17.146917"
   },
   {
    "id": "it_7ea41f474386",
    "card": "live_notes",
    "text": "Presenter wrapping up; will share links to three papers: sector-based localization/detection, deciding whether somebody is active, and clustering of locations over time. A single fixed threshold is a problem across environments (cafeteria, library); current calibration has each person speak in front of the mic and subtracts the level kept in the other mics. A single-channel calibration paper with code online was offered.",
    "data": {
     "heading": "Wrap-up: paper links and calibration",
     "start_s": 802.1
    },
    "status": "proposed",
    "author_type": "agent",
    "author_id": "agent",
    "pinned": false,
    "revision": 1,
    "evidence": [
     "sg_5d75b0cccaa9c41ccd2c",
